<h1>Joan E. Powell</h1>
<p>Judge up for retention, on the Chicago ballot November 3, 2026. Incumbent.</p>
<p>Circuit Court of Cook County</p>
<h2>Ratings</h2>
<ul>
<li>Chicago Bar Association: <a href="https://www.chicagobar.org/votejudges#:~:text=Joan%20E.%20Powell" rel="nofollow noopener">Qualified</a></li>
<li>Illinois State Bar Association: <a href="https://www.isba.org/judicial-elections/counties/cook#:~:text=Joan%20E.%20Powell" rel="nofollow noopener">Yes</a></li>
<li>Injustice Watch: <a href="https://2026retention.injusticewatch.org/candidate/joan-e-powell-35867" rel="nofollow noopener">Notable reversals</a></li>
</ul>
<h2>Record</h2>
<p>Appointed to the Circuit Court in 2006 and elected in 2008; sits in the Law Division, presiding over civil trials. Injustice Watch reports that in 2025 the appellate court vacated a $43.8 million jury verdict in a car crash case she heard and ordered a new trial before a different judge, finding she should have questioned jurors one by one about a blog post by the plaintiff&#39;s attorneys. She told Injustice Watch she followed the Illinois Supreme Court jury instructions and now polls jurors individually when issues arise. A judge stays on the bench with a yes from 60 percent of voters.</p>
<h2>Background</h2>
<p>Cook County assistant state&#39;s attorney in the complex litigation division (2000-2006); earlier a law clerk for two Cook County circuit judges (1996-2000) and a solo practitioner in contract, family, and elder law (1992-1996). Law degree from UIC Law (formerly John Marshall Law School) (1992).</p>
